<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  RUT_WalkerSurfacing.xml                UtinniPatches · SCALD_MECHANICS_1 S5
  ============================================================================
  scald_kit_spec.md S5 "bottom-walkers": "RUT_WalkerSurfacing IncidentDef
  (weighted only into this biome, cooldown days INVENTED: 8-20) +
  RUT_IncidentWorker_WalkerSurfacing." The worker itself was BUILT AND
  COMPILING in this item's own earlier spike pass
  (RUT_IncidentWorker_WalkerSurfacing.cs,
  src/RimMandrake/EnvironmentalHazards/Source/, read in full before writing
  this file); that pass explicitly left "the real RUT_WalkerSurfacing
  IncidentDef XML and its cooldown tuning" owed to the full build. This file
  ships it — completing the bottom-walker half of S5.

  category Misc, allowedBiomes RUT_TheScald — same shape RUT_Surge.xml
  (MIASMA_MECHANICS_1 M2, this same folder) already established for "an
  incident weighted only into one biome": Misc keeps it out of the vanilla
  Storyteller's ThreatSmall/ThreatBig queues (this is atmosphere, not a
  threat, same reasoning RUT_ContagionProbe.xml/RUT_FeverWood_MirrorBreak.xml
  already give); allowedBiomes (a real, confirmed vanilla IncidentDef field,
  RUT_Surge.xml's own header cites it against the live decompile) rejects
  CanFireNow on every non-Scald map.

  minRefireDays 14 — the spec's own "8-20" INVENTED range collapses to its
  midpoint as a single float (IncidentDef.minRefireDays has no range type;
  confirmed, RimWorld/IncidentDef.cs:28, read this pass), the same "a range
  narrated in prose becomes one picked value" collapse this item's own S6
  pass already used for its wreck-count "1-2" -> count 1. baseChance 1.0
  (INVENTED) — the low end of this mod's own established range for
  "ambient atmosphere beat, no bespoke gate beyond the biome" incidents
  (RUT_ContagionProbe 1.5, RUT_FeverWood_MirrorBreak 1.2): a rare distant
  sighting is lower-stakes than either of those two.

  No letter fields set: RUT_IncidentWorker_WalkerSurfacing.TryExecuteWorker
  fires a Messages.Message itself, not a Letter — the spec's own words,
  "Message not Letter after the first sighting." An IncidentDef's own
  letterLabel/letterText fields feed the DEFAULT IncidentWorker.
  PostFireResult path this custom worker's own override never calls, so
  leaving them unset is correct, not an oversight.

  MayRequire mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards: workerClass lives there.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Defs>

  <IncidentDef MayRequire="mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards">
    <defName>RUT_WalkerSurfacing</defName>
    <label>walker surfacing</label>
    <targetTags>
      <li>Map_PlayerHome</li>
    </targetTags>
    <category>Misc</category>
    <workerClass>RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.RUT_IncidentWorker_WalkerSurfacing</workerClass>
    <baseChance>1.0</baseChance>
    <minRefireDays>14</minRefireDays>
    <allowedBiomes>
      <li>RUT_TheScald</li>
    </allowedBiomes>
  </IncidentDef>

</Defs>
